<urn:sha256:29e9519c86247fcc6919d73fcd1276eb43336ec6b228d6d54487e2e46d8fdd32> <urn:ledger:ns#statement> "An operator makes what it keeps for an execution the first time it is opened in it and keeps it on the operator: a BGP's cursor, which its Dispose hands back for the next Open, the join keys, the resolved VALUES rows, the GRAPH name and the named graphs; so the right side of a bind join pays for them once per execution, not once per left solution" <urn:varve-spike:g/ledger> .
